# 🧪 Practical Lab

If you have a Linux VM, first check whether the SSH client is available:

```bash
ssh -V
```

Check whether an SSH server is running:

```bash
systemctl status ssh
```

On some distributions the service may be named:

```bash
systemctl status sshd
```

Check whether port 22 is listening:

```bash
ss -tln | grep :22
```

Generate a test SSH key pair:

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519
```

⚠️ Do this only in your own lab environment. Never experiment against systems you do not own or have permission to test.

